{
  "name": "v10_vec_bank",
  "description": "fnet v10 component 2: the 12-register vector bank (one-combinator registers + write heads + read mux) driven entirely through chunk1's green memory bus. Proves direct frame write, register-to-register copy through the mux, the FREE vector ADD (R and S both selected, frames sum on the shared write bus), R=S selecting a source once rather than twice, per-block erase, the far end of the bank, the one-tick MOVE primitive (erase+write same tick = replace), and that all four op-farm operand faces (pair A = VREG0 x VREG1, pair B = VREG2 x VREG3) carry what they should - plus pair B's OPPOSITE faces a2g/b2r, which are what let the op farm square a single register with the ordinary each[red] x each[green] shape. The widening to 12 (from 8) is exercised at both ends of the new range: block 12 writes, reads back and erases without disturbing block 9. Registers own mux indices 1..16 with ops from 17, so four more registers can be added later without renumbering anything. Timing rules baked into the step order: a select is PARKED and a mux-sourced write is PULSED; DESELECT LAGS, so changing selects and pulsing W together commits the PREVIOUS selection (caught live 2026-07-27 - VREG7 captured VREG0's stale frame), hence the explicit deselect-settle steps; a DIRECT frame write needs no park, because control and data are in phase with no mirror stage.",
